Z||000000||FiXXXerX||12-31-2001||03:12 PM||||Why when I start the car is there white smoke coming from the TBI unit and sometimes, shooting from the small rubber piece that airates the oil rocker cover? I fixed the TBI so that now it sprays into the engine, but I can't get it to run by itself, well, I did once.... but not since then. And it also seems to "Breathe" somtimes after trying to start it, by Breatheing I mean, is seems to sigh, and puff the white smoke out. Nothing smells like its burning or anything, in fact, the smoke doesn't smell like much at all. I've changed the spark plugs, (Haven't done the wires yet, or the Distributor cap or Rotor), what could it be? It sounds like it wants to start, but it just won't do it, then it does that "Breatheing" thing. Its a 4cly 4speed, installed new Autolite Sparkplugs into it and have a used injector installed as well.<BR>I wondered if maybe something was wrong with the oil or somthing along those lines... This car was previously owned by someone who seemed not to know what they were doing, or didn't car about the vehicle. So, any ideas about what the problem is would be welcome. If you need any more info that I failed to give, just ask me.<P>Adam<P>------------------<BR>-= If the Front wheels don't leave the ground, its still broken =-||||reg||5
